    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the lineup as the clear standout play (73.66). Facing off against the relatively hittable Gavin Holmes (4.71 xERA), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost and a prime #2 lineup spot, making him the highest-ceiling asset on the board. Beyond him, **Jacob Wilson** (59.39) and **Kyle Tucker** (59.83) provide excellent production floors. **Jacob Wilson** is aided by a 10% park factor bump, while **Kyle Tucker** is buoyed by favorable wind conditions at the park today, which helps mitigate the challenge of facing a solid arm in Bryan Woo.\n\nThe decision-making process for the final outfield and middle infield spots was tight, particularly regarding **Luis Robert Jr.** (48.05). Despite his elite potential, he was downgraded significantly by a -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Eury P\u00e9rez, keeping him just behind the likes of **Heliot Ramos** (57.51) and **Andy Pages** (57.01) in the rotation. **Sam Antonacci** stood out as the most interesting \"near-miss\" on the bench; while his underlying metrics are solid, he was ultimately excluded due to the optimizer projecting him as a non-starter for today\u2019s contest.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, as the rain threat (32%) in the games involving **Liam Hicks**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** warrants close monitoring throughout the afternoon. Furthermore, the lineup status for **Jacob Wilson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Andy Pages** remains pending; while these projections assume their positions, any late-scratch or tactical rest day could necessitate an immediate pivot to our bench depth. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while the absences of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** due to scheduling leave us relying on the current active roster to carry the load against these specific arms.",
